  "patch_sha256": "b778381f979c0b4ad07b5432f61be7967ecf69c53e47bbf4faada0faa5ac7b71",
  "root_cause": "Source navigation called ReviewBackend._row -> Inventory.candidate. A stale global group revision made that read synchronously wait for group_lock and regroup behind unrelated automatic source/media work. The HTTP route itself has no operation_lock; actual shell dispatch is direct argument-vector explorer Popen, no IPC/openPath promise. UI request previously had no deadline.",
  "fix": "Catalog-only guarded source-folder paths read with no regroup/writer/group/review/operation lock; configured-root, archive, opaque-ID, selected-directory and native ancestry protections remain. Finite30s request with3s waiting copy, actual typed access refusal, unknown outcome copy, per-generation attempt state, retry and duplicate suppression; no focus move.",
  "proof": "Baseline dispatch occurred after worker release (0.525988 vs0.505951s). Corrected freeze dispatch0.012297s while worker still held group/review/operation locks (release0.012325s). Actual Handler.do_POST/token/admission path also passes with Explorer mocked. Final7 casesPASS2.872s, owned3.660s/nativezero;3 frontend scriptsPASS.",
  "preserved_failures": "Wrong selector loader in folder-http-1 retained; corrected selector passes. Broad folder-final-1 had12/15PASS and3 unrelated Tolkien approval cases refusing >240char paths under the long private fixture root; no path policy change. Direct affected folder case and all7 frozen selectors pass.",
  "commands": [
    "node <owned-scratch>/owned.mjs folder-freeze-1 test_lock_timing.SourceFolderDispatchTests test_merge_http.MergeHTTPTests.test_inspection_and_folder_use_only_opaque_record_identity test_merge_service.MergeTests.test_folder_action_uses_opaque_catalog_identity_and_mock_dispatch test_destination_override.OpenFolderTests test_folder_regroup.FolderRegroupTests.test_order_question_says_membership_is_settled_and_rows_say_where_their_files_are"
  ],
  "scope": "Private fixtures/mock Explorer only; no live app/focus/open action. Read-only source diagnostics were a separately authorized batch with independently preserved evidence and completed scoped cleanup.",
